Verified assertions:
- `setupOpenCodeV2Harness({directory:''})` NO-THROW, `workspaceRoot == process.cwd()` ✓
- `setupOpenCodeV2Harness({directory:'   '})` NO-THROW ✓
- `setupOpenCodeV2Harness({worktree:''})` NO-THROW ✓
- `resolveHarnessOptions({rootDir:''})` THROWS fail-closed ✓
- `resolveHarnessOptions({rootDir:'   '})` THROWS fail-closed ✓

Also verified `src/index.ts` contains the `pick()` guard:
```ts
const pick = (v: unknown): string | undefined =>
  typeof v === "string" && v.trim() !== "" ? v : undefined;
const inferredRoot =
  pick(ctx?.directory) ??
  pick(ctx?.worktree) ??
  pick(ctx?.location?.directory) ??
  pick(ctx?.location?.worktree) ??
  process.cwd();
```

## 3. Red-proof sabotage tests (prove the suite FAILS when code is broken)

### S1: revert `pick()` guard → broken `??`-only chain
- Sabotage command: replaced the `pick()`-guarded `inferredRoot` chain in
  `src/index.ts` with the broken form:
  `ctx?.directory ?? ctx?.worktree ?? ctx?.location?.directory ?? ctx?.location?.worktree ?? process.cwd()`
  → `S1-SABOTAGE-APPLIED`
- Check command: `bun test test/p0-1-empty-directory.test.ts`
- Result: **EXIT 1 — 2 pass, 7 fail** (RED as required, proves new tests catch the bug):
```
error: expect(received).not.toThrow()
Error message: "opencode-harness: rootDir must be a non-empty string (fail-closed)"
(fail) P0-1 empty-directory guard > setup({ directory: '\t\n ' }) whitespace-only falls back to process.cwd()
 2 pass
 7 fail
S1-EXIT:1
```
- Restore: `cp /tmp/p01-index-fixed.ts src/index.ts` → `cmp` identical → `S1-RESTORE-OK`
- Re-green: `bun test test/p0-1-empty-directory.test.ts` → **9 pass, 0 fail, EXIT 0**

